# the -f builtin to the declare(typeset) builtin command lists function names and definitions. The -F option 
#to declare or typeset lists function names only. Functions may be exported so that child shell processes
#automatically have them defined with the -f option to the export builtin. The -f option to the unset builtin 
#deletes a function definition.
#Functions can be recursive; use the FUNCNEST variable to limit the depth of the function call stack and
