#appends to or adds to the variable's previous value. This includes arguments to declaration commands such as 
#declare that accept assignment statements. When += is applied to a variable for which the integer attribute has
# been set, the variable's current value and value are each evaluated as arithmetic expressions, and the sum of the 
#results is assigned as the variable's value.The current value is usually an integer constant, but can be an 
#expression. When += is applied to an array variable using compound assignment, the variable's value is not unset,
# and new values are appended to the array beginning at one greater than the array's maximum index, or added 
#as key value pairs in an associative array. When applied to a string-valued variable, value is expanded and
